    "The rankings differ across the two models because Elastic Net and Random Forest use the predictors in different ways. Elastic Net is a regularized linear model, so predictor importance is tied to linear effects after shrinkage. Random Forest is more flexible and can assign importance to predictors that matter through nonlinear patterns or interactions. Differences in the rankings therefore reflect differences in model structure, not only differences in predictive strength.\n",
