    "The Random Forest importance results suggest that portfolio performance is mainly driven by state-dependent valuation, volatility, and size effects. The largest Sharpe-ratio drop comes from `characteristic_ep_x_macro_bm`, indicating that the predictive value of earnings-to-price depends on aggregate book-to-market conditions. This is consistent with value-based return predictability varying across market valuation states.\n",
